  "passage": "A history class watched an old newsreel from wartime. The music was dramatic, and the narrator spoke with great confidence.\nAt first, students accepted it as information. Then the teacher asked them to identify persuasion techniques. They noticed selective images, emotional language, and missing viewpoints.\nThe class learned that historical media can be both evidence and propaganda.\nThe newsreel showed what people were told, not necessarily the whole truth.\nStudents realized media literacy is not only for modern social media. People have always used images and sound to shape public feeling. Critical viewing is a historical skill as much as a modern one.",
